dependent post-cleanup audit has its own250ms budget. No removed50ms cap reappears.\", \"A late STOP acknowledgement can leave less than80ms plus actual ps/parsing/census work. Even>80ms remaining does not guarantee a further required stable census. That is conditional budget arithmetic; no retained failed log supplies the actual remaining time or proves this path.\", \"An incomplete quiescence clears prior census history and requires two complete stable quiet censuses by the original deadline. A successful final drain cannot erase a retained quiescence error. Actual root wait precedes final drain; cleanup receipttrue requires all required proof. No actionable wrong-acceptance or orphan mechanism demonstrated.\", \"The same timeout string can originate from injected scan3, later cleanup scans or the separate final audit. Generic raw timeout and prior recovery text cannot select among them.\"], \"status\": \"OPEN\", \"why_no_speculative_fix\": \"Moving/deleting the80ms injection or audit, padding deadlines or imposing artificial lateness would not establish which requirement failed. Existing forced deadline controls validate ownership and classification, not the retained natural trigger.\"}, \"evidence_receipt\": \".cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-10/owner-terminal-assessment/owner-terminal-assessment.json\", \"next_action\": {\"command\": \"cargo test --locked -p bd-cache-sync --test cron_hurry --all-features -- --nocapture\", \"context_limit\": \"Package-selected run restores the existing lifecycle test-family context on the instrumented C2 consumer; it does not reproduce the entire original workspace feature union/build artifact or scheduling interleaving. Record that limitation. If a previously consumer-workspace-built matching instrumented artifact is already available, invoke that full target once with --nocapture instead of building/running a broader matrix; do not execute both alternatives.\", \"execution\": \"Recommended for parent dispatch; nothing promoted, prepared or executed by this reviewer.\", \"experiment_count\": 1, \"not_authorized_by_this_assessment\": \"No retry-to-green, synthetic host load, forced-lateness counterexample, thread override, timer widening, removing/moving the fault/audit, full1171 matrix, SDK/publisher/auth changes, waiver, PR approval or merge.\", \"on_failure\": \"Use the identified actual stage/call/remaining and ownership receipt to route a concrete fixture/inventory correction. Preserve original100ms/250ms/1s/5s budgets,80ms fault, complete census, false incomplete receipts and one attempt until a supported redesign is reviewed.\", \"on_success\": \"Record actual stage/timing/control coverage and stop. A success is not the historical cause or correction; no automatic unchanged rerun/stress loop. Owner may assess source/control proof or another specifically justified causal action from the new facts; no requirement to wait indefinitely for an identical historical event.\", \"platform\": \"native hosted macOS\", \"required_records\": \"Literal immutable source/checkout and helper blob, consumer lock/feature selection and actual cron_hurry binary/hash, full count/command/environment, raw stageBEGIN/END including original deadline and remaining time, STOPack/delay/CONT of injected call3, actual inventoryPID exit or kill/wait, rootwait, complete stable/final census, cleanup receipt and independent audit. Preserve actual test outcome and all errors.\", \"scope\": \"Ordinarily consume immutable ec68 producer diagnostics into C2, preserving consumer production, manifests/lock, validated store protocol and complete prior histories. Record new immutable consumer SHA and verify Rust delta is the intended SessionFixture diagnostics/control only; do not mix a speculative correction.\", \"selection\": \"Exactly the existing full cron_hurry integration target after diagnostic consumption, expected19 tests. No original-case --exact filter: retain default parent concurrency and existing sibling conte